<title>GERMANY: Waigel/Tietmeyer share view on talks outcome - Bub.</title>
<headline>Waigel/Tietmeyer share view on talks outcome - Bub.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-06-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Comments made by Bundesbank president Hans Tietmeyer and Finance Minister Theo Waigel on the outcome of talks held in Bonn on Tuesday correspond with each other, a Bundesbank spokesman said.</p>
<p>There was no disagreement on the results achieved, he said.</p>
<p>&quot;There was no difference between the statements made by Mr. Tietmeyer and Mr. Waigel,&quot; he said, adding that his comment was a response to market talk that the two were at odds over the outcome of Tuesday's meeting.</p>
<p>Earlier, the Bundesbank dismissed press reports that Tietmeyer had denied he had an agreement with Waigel over the revaluation of Bundesbank reserves. The central bank said that no formal agreement had been reached, adding appropriate bodies had yet to give their approval.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
